{
  "_about": "What a board needs to play in the phone app's local webview (tools/phone-board.mjs ships exactly this, mirrored under the skill's own paths — a game's `new URL('../../worlds/…', import.meta.url)` keeps working untouched). `entry` pages: the host page (scripts/games/phone/). `shared`: what every board's page loads (the sound kit; lingjing.css, whose :root holds the colours and type every board's CSS reads). `games.<id>`: the game's module, its own folders (bundle, engine, art, font), the shared files it names by URL, and the JS it loads through its static imports (found by walking them — never listed); `css` the sheets the host page links before it mounts (shipped too). `exclude`: build leftovers inside a game folder. `dynamic`: modules a game loads on demand, not shipped in its own pack (the camera 结印 is its own pack, `jieyin`, which the app loads when a board first asks for it — 10-27; with no camera the dock is never offered, and every board is the board without it). Packs (phone-board.mjs --all): one `common` (the entry, `shared`, and every file two or more boards need) and one per game (the rest of its own); the app answers a path from whichever pack holds it. Step 1 of doc/lingjing-phone.md (linggen-mobile): 第一回's boards.",
